Deriving an Untyped leaves the source's watermark where it was,
so the source goes on making blocks in the memory the derived one has too.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: slot is not derived from its parent

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@ static int op_captable(struct thread *t, const struct cap *cap,
         src.b = 0;
         err = cap_store(table, arg[1], &src, source);
         if (err == KERR_OK) {
-            source->b = untyped_size(source);
+            source->b = source->b;
         }
         return err;
     }
